  "summary": "Every read of a rendered document now sees one immutable document: Plite createEditorView(editor, { document }) binds reads, plugin reads and APIs to it, replacing the partial Plate facade, and a guard refuses source-editor reads made on a document view's behalf. HTML claims only what its output keeps and reports every other property. Static rendering reuses a block while it and every earlier block are unchanged and its decorations are value-equal; elements that read later content declare render.readsDocument (the TOC). Five wrong-document reads were fixed at their owners (code highlight, find, Markdown serialize, the AI end marker and Plite node targets), plus a Plite portal refresh that rebuilt the plugin configuration per lookup.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "verified",
    "evidence": [
